    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling performance tonight, spearheaded by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.72) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages a favorable matchup against Rea, bolstered by park and skill factors, while **Sam Antonacci** earns top-tier status due to his leadoff spot and a lucrative matchup against Melton. **Jacob Wilson** (67.53) also represents an elite start; the combination of a high-value lineup spot and a +10% park factor makes him an essential piece. **Kyle Tucker** (66.82) and **Andy Pages** (66.58) provide strong production against Rogers, with the latter benefiting from the starter\u2019s slow delivery, which creates prime conditions for stolen bases\u2014a critical component of our strategy given our emphasis on speed.\n\nWhile **Nolan Schanuel** (57.80) nearly cracked the starting nine, his lack of high-leverage context compared to the consistency of **Miguel Vargas** (61.67) and **Gunnar Henderson** (61.23) ultimately relegated him to the bench. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a focal point despite the difficulty of facing Yamamoto; his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) keeps his floor elevated even against elite competition. Conversely, caution is warranted for **Jackson Merrill** (49.51) and **Drake Baldwin** (50.38), both of whom are hovering near the marginal tier. **Jackson Merrill** is specifically hampered by a negative platoon shift (-13%), and while he offers some upside due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s inability to hold runners, he remains a candidate for mid-game substitution if the Waves build an early lead. Monitor weather reports for all venues, but otherwise, the lineup is optimized to maximize both raw output and the pursuit of elite speed targets.",
